Articulate – able to express ideas clearly
Example: She is very articulate in meetings.*


Baffle – to confuse someone
Example: The puzzle baffled him.*


Coherent – clear and logical
Example: His explanation was coherent.*


Derive – to get something from a source
Example: Many words derive from Latin.*


Elusive – hard to find or understand
Example: Success can be elusive.*


Fluctuate – to change frequently
Example: Prices fluctuate every day.*


Grim – serious or gloomy
Example: The situation looks grim.*


Hasty – done too quickly
Example: He made a hasty decision.*


Insight – deep understanding
Example: The book gave great insight.*


Jargon – special words used by a group
Example: Technical jargon can be confusing.*



